//@version=6
indicator("UCTPROBE_VW_BARSTATE_FORMING", overlay = false)

// PROVENANCE: written 2026-11-21 (Q-BSF, docs/pine/capture-queue-2026-11-23-barstate-forming.md), for the
// FORMING-bar witness of `realtime-state` (rollout_gate.PINE_CAPABILITY_FORMING_UNGRADED): today every capture that
// admits it holds a FINISHED newest bar, so the capability is served for closed-bar history only (scope
// closed-bar-history) and the member door refuses it by name on a chart whose newest bar is forming.
// The only committed barstate capture, `barstate-full-spy-1d-closed-2026-09-10`, is a closed chart.
// NEVER COMPILED ON TRADINGVIEW.
//
// ─── WHAT EACH barstate VARIABLE READS ON EVERY BAR, THE NEWEST ONE FORMING ───
//
// Captured in regular hours, so the newest bar is a realtime bar that has not closed. Expected on that bar:
// isconfirmed 0, isrealtime 1, islast 1, ishistory 0, islastconfirmedhistory 0 (it is 1 on the bar BEFORE).
// Every historical bar reads isconfirmed 1, isrealtime 0, ishistory 1. The engine must draw exactly these columns,
// bar for bar.
//
//   F00          bar_index (control: which bar a row is)
//   F01          barstate.isconfirmed            as 1 / 0
//   F02          barstate.isrealtime             as 1 / 0
//   F03          barstate.islast                 as 1 / 0
//   F04          barstate.ishistory              as 1 / 0
//   F05          barstate.islastconfirmedhistory as 1 / 0
//   F06          barstate.isconfirmed ? close : na   (a VALUE that depends on the state: a community shape)
//   F07          close (control: reads no state)
//
// NOT HERE: `barstate.isnew`. Both lanes refuse it by name (pine:builtin, RULING-0927: it needs per-tick evaluation),
// and a refused line would withhold the whole probe (language probe 2026-11-21). Its forming-bar witness is the
// community visualizer row (Q-BSF-e), graded refused, for a future per-tick unit.

plot(bar_index, "F00")
plot(barstate.isconfirmed ? 1 : 0, "F01")
plot(barstate.isrealtime ? 1 : 0, "F02")
plot(barstate.islast ? 1 : 0, "F03")
plot(barstate.ishistory ? 1 : 0, "F04")
plot(barstate.islastconfirmedhistory ? 1 : 0, "F05")
plot(barstate.isconfirmed ? close : na, "F06")
plot(close, "F07")
